|section=
|text=Unsustainable development threatens the health and diverse fish populations of the '''Mekong''' river, with one-fifth of fish species in Southeast Asia's main artery facing extinction, a report by conservation groups said on Monday.<br>The '''Mekong''', stretching nearly 5,000 km (3,000 miles) from the Tibetan Plateau to the South China Sea, is a farming and fishing lifeline for tens of millions of people in China, Laos, Myanmar, Thailand, Cambodia and Vietnam.}}
